  "body": "## Summary\n\nCommand Code's Provider API exposes one live model catalog across two incompatible inference routes. Claude models require native Anthropic Messages; OpenAI and open-source models require Chat Completions. This PR adds one first-class `commandcode/...` provider that routes each family correctly instead of falsely advertising the whole catalog through one transport.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `COMMANDCODE_API_KEY`, proxy, multi-key pool/rotation, health/status, model discovery and admin-card integration.\n- Added a neutral native Anthropic Messages upstream family with request preservation, validated SSE pass-through, pre-commit retry/holdback, canonical failures and cleanup.\n- Added a hybrid Command Code adapter: `claude-*` uses `/provider/v1/messages`; all other live-catalog IDs use `/provider/v1/chat/completions`.\n- Preserved catalog `context_length` metadata without inventing unsupported capability flags.\n- Added v4.54.0 docs, env, smoke and exhaustive provider contracts.\n\n## Verification\n\n```text\nruff format --check: 528 files already formatted\nruff check: All checks passed\nuv run ty check: All checks passed\nTargeted provider/admin/runtime suite: 108 passed\nNon-installer suite with external EXA_API_KEY cleared: 3548 passed, 1 skipped\nBrowser: Command Code card rendered on isolated Windows port 8148 with key, rotation and proxy fields; 0 console warnings/errors; all 10 admin requests HTTP 200\n```\n\nThe unfiltered local full suite reported pre-existing/environmental failures: externally configured `EXA_API_KEY` changed web-search defaults, PowerShell installer checksum mocks failed, and uninstaller tests detected a real running `fcc-claude`. None involve files changed here; clearing EXA made the affected web-search tests pass. Port 8082 was not touched.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Live model discovery was verified against the public `/models` endpoint, but live inference was not called because no Command Code Provider-plan key was available.\n- Command Code documents its current Claude IDs as `claude-*`; the route predicate deliberately follows that narrow documented/catalog convention rather than guessing vendor aliases.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
