    },
    "message": "feat: add Command Code dual-protocol provider\n\nCommand Code exposes one live catalog across two incompatible inference paths: Claude models require native Anthropic Messages while every other advertised model uses OpenAI Chat Completions. Treating it as a generic OpenAI gateway would silently advertise models that always fail.\n\nAdd a hybrid provider that dispatches claude-* IDs to a reusable native Messages transport and delegates the rest to the existing OpenAI chat adapter. The catalog, admin card, key pools, rotation, health, proxy, discovery context metadata, fallback boundaries, and smoke configuration remain under FCC's normal provider contracts.\n\nVerified with Ruff format/check, ty, 108 targeted tests, 3,548 non-installer tests, protocol-faithful fake upstream streams, and browser inspection of the v4.54.0 Command Code card on isolated port 8148. Live completion remains unverified without a Provider-plan key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
